       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen at 9,000 mg/day is a hepatotoxic dose, and I don't know of any indication that justifies it in a 70 kg adult. Harm is likely, and the risk doesn't depend on normal baseline liver function.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter a dose within the safe range right away, such as 1,000 mg PO three or four times daily. The maximum is 4,000 mg/day.\n- Help with a different analgesic plan if pain control is the problem.\n- If you think this order is justified, such as a protocol I'm not aware of or a typo in the intended drug, take it to pharmacy or your institution's order-verification process. They can review and enter it outside my workflow.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like entered, and I'll enter it now."
